# A point-to-point move with limited acceleration: the trapezoidal speed profile.
part trapezoid_move "Trapezoidal move (limited acceleration)"
category Control
summary "A commanded angle that speeds up at a set acceleration, cruises, and slows down to stop exactly at the target."
explain "The commanded speed follows a trapezoid: it rises at `accel` from `start`, is capped at `rate`, and falls at `accel` so it reaches zero after travelling `travel`. The angle is its integral. Starting a stepper or a servo this way keeps the torque it needs to accelerate the load within what it can give."
tradeoffs "Gentler acceleration asks for less torque but makes the move take longer. The fastest move within a motor's torque uses the largest acceleration it can reliably deliver with margin."
limits "Moves forward only (travel > 0); the slow-down begins from the remaining distance, so a move too short to reach `rate` becomes a triangle."
pairs part.stepper_motor part.pid_angle robot.effective_servo robot.servo_firmware
output angle Angle
param travel rad ~ 6.283185307 "Distance to move"
param rate rad/s ~ 60 "Cruise speed"
param accel rad/s^2 ~ 600 "Acceleration and deceleration"
param start s = 0 "When the move starts"
param edge s = 0.0002 "Smoothing of the start, and of the final approach (keeps the stop solvable)"
state moved Angle = 0
let left = max(travel - moved, 0)
let soft = accel*edge
let speed = max(0, min(min(rate, accel*max(t - start, 0)), sqrt(2*accel*left + soft*soft) - soft))
eq der(moved) = speed*0.5*(1 + tanh((t - start)/edge))
set angle = moved
derive "time to reach cruise speed" = rate/accel s
